upload a game
==============
git pull origin master
npm run build
go to s3 in every game and press Upload
choose everything from the dist folder under the relevant subfolder
go to the folderin s3 with the uploaded files (press on the destination link), check all of them , press actoions --> make public
go to the bottom of the page and press "Make Public"


add new game to reability DB
-----------------------------------
in heroku reability open settings tab and press on "Reveal Config Vars"
change the SCRIPT_BUCKET_NAME to the name of the new game's bucket
change the  SCRIPT_GAME_NAME to the name that will be shown in the UI
in htrko press the More button and choose Run Console
in the heroku console write: npm run db:add:game


add a new game in amazone s3
-----------------------------
in the main s3 screen press on "Create Bucket"
give name: gertner-<game name>-<environment>
for example: gertnet-mygame-staging

choose to copy from another bucket and choose the memory game

uncheck "block all public access"

check "I acknoledge"

press on the Create button

go to the folder and add the disable.png and enable.png files - these are the icon files of the game in the lobby

proceed with regular upload game flow 

since s3 doesn't allow to upload folders (like assets) you should select all files and folders from the dist and drag them .

special case - no place in amazon - limit 100 buckets
=======================================================
if there are 100 buckets you need to send gil an email with the list of all 100 buckets and ask him which to remove
for every bucket , mark it , press "Empty"  and only after that go back mark it again and press delete.


special case - external company 
===================================
external company must know the the enable disable images must be in the main folder
in addition we need to grant them permissions to the s3 bucket
the external company must have amazone s3 account that has canonicial ID and they must provide it to us.
go to the s3 buccket --> permissions tab --> scroll down to Acess Control List (ACL) and press "Edit" 
scroll to "Access for other AWS accounts" and press "Add Grantee"
put the cononicial id that you got from them  and check all options  and press on ""Save Changes" at the bottom



special case on first time upload to production
=================================================

go to games table in db  and change the new game url to be in the same format as the others
because we use cdn url.

